speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, I wish to present another petition which meets the requirements of the provisions of Standing Order 106.
Whereas the federal Government has imposed 25 new taxes or tax increases on Canadian taxpayers since September 1984, in particular on medical and dental supplies, snack foods, candy and soft drinks;
Whereas the federal Government in its tax reform proposal is studying the possibility of imposing on Canadians a general tax on goods and services, including food;
Whereas food constitutes a vital element in day-to-day life and the imposition of this tax would have the effect of seriously penalizing various categories of taxpayers such as the elderly, families, the unemployed, low and middle income taxpayers, and youth;
Wherefore your petitioners humbly call upon Parliament to reject all measures that would have the effect of imposing a sales tax on food products.
